 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 242425,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/010b40f5e4b4d0d1.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by John A. Vucetich/The Wolves and Moose of Isle Royale)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The graph shows the wolf and moose populations in Isle Royale, a protected national park in Michigan. Wolves are the main predator of moose, but there are many other factors at play.</p>\n<p>Some time during the time frame covered by this graph, humans accidentaly introduced canine parvovirus, a wolf disease to the wolf population.</p>\n<p>When did this event most likely occur?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 759161,
     "content_html": "Between 1969 and 1974."
    },
    {
     "id": 759160,
     "content_html": "Between 1974 and 1979."
    },
    {
     "id": 759162,
     "content_html": "Between 1979 and 1984."
    },
    {
     "id": 759159,
     "content_html": "Between 1984 and 1989."
    }
   ],
